<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-577] ASCII control character errors in Zeppelin</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-577</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;My Zeppelin notebook was throwing some &#8220;sql interpreter not found&#8221; exceptions on code that has worked before. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Investigating the issue it looks like when you paste from an ASCII  character set the cell in Zeppelin uses the ASCII control characters.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This means if I go to the top of the pasted content and add my interpreter and a few new lines I&#8217;ll get a &#8220;sql interpreter not found&#8221; because my cell in the json file is actually:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&quot;text&quot;: &quot;%sql\r\nSELECT\r\n    STORE_NBR\r\nFROM pss_subset_primary_key_hy_2\r\nWHERE START_TXN_DATE \u003d \u00272015-01-03\u0027\r\nlimit 10 &quot;,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I can even get the code to work by adding a space after the interpreter is defined&#8230;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&quot;text&quot;: &quot;%sql \r\nSELECT\r\n    STORE_NBR\r\nFROM pss_subset_primary_key_hy_2\r\nWHERE START_TXN_DATE \u003d \u00272015-01-03\u0027\r\nlimit 10 &quot;,&lt;/p&gt;

